comments.body:
@Henry Don’t worry. Canada is passing on American travel, tomatoes, soup, and vehicles assembled there.

Something about a thinly-veiled threat of being taken over as a ‘‘51st state’’ may have had a hand in that.

And then there’s the widening fork in the road of human and civil rights. Canada is choosing to stay on the main path.

@Alexis it doesn’t have to end at I

This is Trump's economy; period. He owns it along with the Republican congress. The Democrats are old news and Trump told everyone he would 'fix' the economy. Well this is Trump's fix. He has rising inflation. He has record deficits. He has used tariffs to push are trading  partners in to the 'arms' of other countries.

Trump and his supporters will try every argument they can to  deflect the fact, it is as fact; Donald Trump and the Republicans in congress have created this mess.

@Ken
Some of us do indeed know what $10/gal gasoline prices would look like. All I can say is, it sounds a lot better than the current overly cheap price that has everyone buying multiple emotional support vehicles and using them to dangerously drive through neighborhoods to buy one item at a store several times per day.

In case you haven't noticed, the world is on fire. It's our home. Maybe we should stop adding cheap gasoline to that fire.

@Born in Chicago

You have not been to China in recent years. They shut dirty coal power plants and only clean coal plants are allowed to be in use. Beijing has a blue sky one hasn't seen in decades. All taxis are EV.

Having said that, climate change is real. US northeast was near 100 degrees last week. I woudl expect the hurricane formation in southeast later this summer due to the high temperature.
